als were analyzed by viable cell counting and multiparameter FCM for the expression of indicated TCR segments, CD4 and CD8. In parallel, the clonal nature (&#x0003e;97% of the family belonged to a single clone) of their expanded T cells was verified by CDR3 length analysis. Results are representative of 17 control and 19 animals with TCE analyzed in this manner.</p></fn><fn id="tfn1"><label>a</label><p>Calculated from percentages obtained by FCM and total spleen cell numbers (trypan blue exclusion counting).</p></fn><fn id="tfn2"><label>b</label><p>Families exhibiting a decrease in representation &#x0003e;1 SD are outlined in bold.</p></fn><fn id="tfn3"><label>c</label><p>Indicates the TCRV&#x003b2; makeup of the TCE (percent of total CD8<sup>+</sup> cells belonging to the TCE is indicated in brackets underneath the animal number).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="tbl2"><label>Table II.</label><caption><p>No Cross-Regulation between V&#x003b2;7 and V&#x003b2;8 Family Members in the CD8 T Cell Compartment</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left">Mouse</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">% F23.1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4">a</xref></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">% V&#x003b2;8.2/8.3</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">% V&#x003b2;8.1</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">Fold reductionV&#x003b2;8.2/8.3</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">% V&#x003b2;7</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">Fold reductionV&#x003b2;7</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">% V&#x003b2;5</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center">Fold reductionV&#x003b2;5</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left">Control 1</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="char" char=".">23.57</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="char" char=".">12.23</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="char" char=".">11.